## Summary

I shipped a production-polished native Apple parity of **`TripReplayCharts`** — 9 files in `apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views/` following the established 9-file surface pattern (precedent: `PowerProfileChart`/`DriveOverviewChart`):

| File | Role |
|---|---|
| `.swift` | Root view — `TSFadeIn` glass card + phase switch (all 6 states) |
| `.Adapter.swift` | Value types, `nearestIndex` (web `nearestIndexByTime`), number formatting, surface slug |
| `.Projection.swift` | Dual-axis domains + secondary-axis rescale/inverse, phase, playhead clamp, VoiceOver |
| `.Model.swift` | P1/S8 source seam + `@Observable` model (owns playhead, seek→`onSeek`), P1/S10 i18n, P1/S11 telemetry |
| `.Chart.swift` | Swift Charts dual-axis area (speed left / power right rescaled) + `#00b4d8` playhead + tap-to-seek + tooltip |
| `.Views.swift` | Header/subtitle/freshness chip, connectivity banner, loading/empty/error, series legend |
| `.Previews.swift` | 6 state previews · `.Tests.swift` 33 tests · `.strings` i18n catalog |

